  "scope": [
    "Reconcile the current public-profile audit into a human-reviewable inventory of retained legacy text findings and all tracked binary files without retaining matched private values in the report.",
    "Classify actual maintainer environment data, synthetic test fixtures, vendored fixtures, and visual artifacts; inspect every tracked PNG for publishability and record digest-bound dispositions.",
    "Recommend the smallest provenance-preserving remediation sequence while keeping Git-history rewriting, repository visibility, version, tag, GitHub Release, npm publication, and announcement outside this Work Item."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The report reconciles the audit totals, rule classes, occurrence counts, unique files, and binary inventory without exposing matched private values.",
    "Every text class has a risk explanation and recommended disposition, including terminal Work Item worktrees, retained artifacts, Evidence details, test fixtures, and vendored fixtures.",
    "Every tracked binary has a SHA-256-bound visual review result or an explicit unresolved reason; aggregate results distinguish safe retention from required regeneration or removal.",
    "The report identifies what Temple can safely automate and isolates only genuinely consequential Human decisions.",
    "Repository verification and Independent QA pass at an exact candidate; no publication or destructive history action occurs."
  ],
